    "notes": {
      "item": "Lincoln’s own initiative, 25 April (N&H vol. 2 p. 38), as provenance only: the option shows no proposer, and the decision has no staff line (B9). A security order through the general-in-chief (3.5, R8), with locked costs on the border Unionists and both Democratic blocs (B5) and a ledger act owed to Congress (0040). Inaction needs no gate cost: it is the absence of the coercive policy. The desk’s neutral rendering and its architecture test are owed before any desk shows this decision."
    }
  }
